cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DRLP: detachment-limited river long profile"
abstract: >-
  Evolves a bedrock river long profile under the detachment-limited stream-power
  law, dz/dt = U - K Q^m S^n, with the implicit outlet-to-upstream sweep of
  Braun and Willett (2013). Erosion is set locally by the flow rather than by a
  divergence of sediment flux, so the model is advective where its
  transport-limited siblings GRLP and SRLP are diffusive: a base-level fall
  travels upstream as a step that keeps its edge instead of spreading and
  flattening. n = 1 is closed-form and exact; general n is solved by Brent's
  method on a dimensionless bracket that is guaranteed by construction. Position
  reaches discharge through three separate transfer functions - Hack's law for
  drainage area, a power-law hydrology, and optionally Leopold's downstream
  hydraulic geometry for width - so each exponent can be asked about on its own.
  Channel width may be folded into m, the standard treatment, or carried
  explicitly as unit stream power.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wickert
    given-names: Andrew D.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9545-3365"
